    "methodNote": "Average number of rooms per person in the housing stock, per NUTS 2 region, OECD's Regional Statistics database (DSD_REG_SOC@DF_HOUSING, MEASURE=ROOMS, UNIT_MEASURE=RO_PS), 2021 — the newest year before a real coverage drop (not gradual reporting lag). A housing-space signal distinct from every OMI price layer on the Italy map and from Eurostat's cost-based housing-overburden layer here: this is about physical space per resident, not price.",
    "grain": "nuts2",
    "kind": "scalar",
    "coverageNote": "Albania has ZERO codes (not an OECD member). The UK reports real data but at a coarser, NUTS-1-shaped grain (11 codes) than this map's NUTS 2 boundaries, so ZERO UK codes match — the same shape as this batch's other NUTS 2 layers. FRANCE is a DIFFERENT and worse gap, checked directly rather than assumed to match: France has NO ROOMS codes at TL2 at all, not even at the coarser grain the foreign-born-share/income/attainment layers still report France at — a genuine absence from this specific dataflow, not a code-matching problem."
